Usually the negative response falls on the token AFTER a descriptive word:
"same thing", "different from", "general rule", "common denominator".
This approximation uses lexical classes, a few familiar collocations, and a
four-token memory for "same ... as". It also handles some Chinese/Japanese
counterparts and the stronger response when a relation word starts a document.
It does not model the component's small, widely scattered token-specific signal.
