'Let me see/know' gives the largest positive response. Other verbs have
smaller responses after 'let', modals, and nearby conditional/time-clause
introducers. The clause signal fades over eight tokens. Modal-adverb
complements, auxiliary participles, and constant-qualified types/casts
give negative responses. "See" and "know" also raise following "that".
A small secondary rule covers time-word compounds in Chinese/Japanese.
Unrecognized tokens predict zero; all history resets at document changes.

The verb columns are ordinary, after 'to', after a modal, and after 'let'.
The numbers are rounded activation estimates from training text.
